# Line endings are LF, everywhere, for everyone.
#
# This repository's `.editorconfig` already declares `end_of_line = lf`, and Prettier's
# default is `lf` — but neither of those constrains what a *checkout* writes. On Windows
# with `core.autocrlf = true`, git materialises CRLF in the working tree while storing
# LF in the repository, so `pnpm format:check` (and therefore `pnpm verify` and CI)
# reported every one of those files. Declaring `eol=lf` here is what makes the checkout
# agree with the repository on every platform, rather than only on Linux.
#
# `text=auto` keeps git's own per-file text/binary detection, so nothing binary is ever
# rewritten or diffed as text.
#
# This changes nothing that is committed: every blob in the repository is already LF, so
# normalising the working tree back to LF is a no-op against the index.
* text=auto eol=lf
